  "text": "## Deep context: Frankie Insights\nRoute: /agents/frankie/insights\nSummary: Frankie reads your full P&L weekly and writes you a CFO-level narrative — what changed, why, and what to do about it.\n\n**What it is** — AI CFO layer on top of the financial data. Writes weekly narratives, flags anomalies, tracks margin trends, and forecasts cash position using Claude as the AI backend.\n\n**How it works** — Frankie reads invoices, bills, payroll_runs, fleet_fuel_logs, and job line items. The weekly brief is generated by an edge function that assembles full financial context and calls Claude with a CFO-level system prompt. Anomaly detection checks job labor over-budget (actual vs estimate > 120%), fuel cost z-score spikes, and AR aging growth week-over-week. Margin trend data pulls from jobs.gross_margin_pct aggregated by week. Cashflow forecast uses ar_due_dates, bill_due_dates, and next_payroll_run_date to project a 4-week cash position. Frankie is entirely read-only — she never creates, updates, or deletes any records.\n\n**Examples**\n- Show me Frankie's report for last week\n- What anomalies did Frankie flag this week?\n- What's my margin trend over the last 12 weeks?\n- What does my cash position look like over the next month?\n- Why did Frankie flag job #041?\n\n**Gotchas (warn the user about these)**\n- Frankie requires at least 4 weeks of job and invoice data before margin trends and cashflow forecasts are meaningful.\n- Anomaly thresholds (e.g., labor over-budget > 120%) are fixed defaults — custom thresholds are set under Frankie → Settings → Thresholds.\n- The weekly brief is generated on a schedule — if you just onboarded mid-week, your first full brief arrives on the next configured delivery day.\n- Frankie reads payroll_runs, not individual time entries — ensure payroll is finalized before her Monday run for accurate numbers.\n- All Frankie data is scoped to your company_id; she never sees data from other tenants.\n\n**FAQs**\n- Q: Can I trigger a Frankie brief on demand instead of waiting for Monday?\n  A: Yes — go to Frankie → Insights and tap \"Generate Now.\" This runs the same edge function on demand and replaces the current week's brief.\n- Q: How does Frankie know my gross margin target?\n  A: You set it under Settings → Goals → Frankie Targets. Without a target, the margin chart still renders but the reference line and alerts are disabled.\n- Q: Does Frankie send alerts outside of the weekly brief?\n  A: Yes — high-severity anomalies (e.g., a large unmatched payment) trigger an immediate in-app notification regardless of the weekly brief schedule.\n- Q: What AI model powers Frankie's narratives?\n  A: Frankie uses Claude via the Anthropic API with a CFO-persona system prompt. The financial context window is assembled server-side in a Supabase edge function before the call.\n\n**Setup steps**\n1. Enable Frankie — Go to Settings → AI Agents → Frankie The AI CFO → Enable. She needs read access to Books, Jobs, Invoices, and Payroll to do her job.\n2. Set financial targets — Navigate to Settings → Goals → Frankie Targets. Enter your gross margin target %, monthly revenue goal, and minimum cash reserve. Frankie compares every week against these.\n3. Configure weekly brief — Under Frankie → Settings → Weekly Brief, choose your delivery day (Monday is recommended) and notification method — in-app, email, or both.\n4. Review anomalies daily — Visit Frankie → Insights → Anomalies each morning. Dismiss false positives and tag real issues as \"Investigating.\" Frankie learns your patterns over time and gets sharper."
